<title>RUSSIA: Chirac-Yeltsin talks extended half an hour.</title>
<headline>Chirac-Yeltsin talks extended half an hour.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Talks between Russian President Boris Yeltsin and French leader Jacques Chirac were extended by 30 minutes on Sunday, Interfax news agency said, quoting well-informed sources.</p>
<p>Interfax said the talks had been extended to allow further discussion of security issues and bilateral relations. Chirac's departure had been rescheduled for 6 p.m. (1500GMT).</p>
